{
 "fix": "#55 fail-closed durability-critical write and fsync failures",
 "merge_commit": "e4647d88",
 "remaining_risks": [
  "EIO injected instead of a real failed fsync; kernel page-cache drop semantics not exercised",
  "power loss emulated only for the page-log tail",
  "one host/filesystem/drive; stress profile needed to reach most sites; production runs the default profile",
  "not covered: open-time failures as counted boundary, HA/quorum/standby (#71), archives (#73), event log, audit outbox, bulk-load/index-build 08007 with commit_seq=none, encrypted stores",
  "transaction_log.cut_copy firing not observable (0 of 10 confirmed)",
  "plain-SIGKILL recovery of server_paged stress stores unreliable at this revision (cross-cutting findings)",
  "verifier unmerged and blind to small secondary-index omissions"
 ],
 "observations": [
  "page_file.write documented not fatal but fenced at paged.commit in 9 of 9 fired trials (fails closed)",
  "transaction_log.sync faults record site transaction_log.write or transaction_log.auxiliary, not the injection name",
  "failed transaction-log sync: embedded resolves not_committed (81/81), paged mostly committed (98/114); consistent with storage, paged case not described in docs section 4",
  "in-workload paged transaction-log cut fault fired 8 of 20; shutdown variant 15 of 20"
 ],
